From ce1f64f961d714dccba61409e6cd12da11933b77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AEON-7 <aeon-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:31:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] [AEON M2] inkling2 gfx12: fuse static short conv with
 the following attn-res mix (T<=8); MoE T=1 retune

- ops/sconv_mix.py (new, AEON): one program per token runs the attn-out /
  mlp-out conv + residual update and then the attn-res mix of that token for
  every query, taking the conv output from registers. -2 launches per layer
  visit (755 -> 611 kernels per bs1 step). AEON_FUSE_SCONV_MIX=0 disables.
- sconv.Inkling2ShortConv.forward_mix; loop._run_layer uses it.
- moe_decode: sort top-k also at T=1; NVFP4 per-row cfg (8,256,1)/(4,128,1).
- o_proj hook point (HOOKS.oproj) unchanged.

gen_bench bs1 78.1, bs8 372.9 tok/s; KL (max-batched 8, exercises T<=8 kernels) 0.00207 / top-1 98.12%.
